--------------------------------------------------

STEP 5: GENERATE SAFE MONGO SHELL SCRIPT

At the end, generate a MongoDB shell script to apply the changes.

Requirements:

1. Script must be SAFE and IDEMPOTENT
2. Use createIndex with options:
   - { background: true, name: "<generated_name>" }
3. DO NOT drop indexes immediately:
   - Instead, COMMENT OUT dropIndex statements
4. Add clear comments for each action
5. Preserve existing indexes unless explicitly marked for deletion
6. For modifications:
   - Create new index first
   - Comment old index for later removal
7. Use consistent index naming convention:
   <field1>_<field2>_<order>

--------------------------------------------------

SCRIPT FORMAT

// Use database
use <db_name>

// ==============================
// Collection: <collection_name>
// ==============================

// Create new indexes
db.<collection>.createIndex(
  { fieldA: 1, fieldB: -1 },
  { name: "fieldA_fieldB_idx", background: true }
)

// Modify index (create new first)
db.<collection>.createIndex(
  { fieldA: 1, fieldC: 1 },
  { name: "fieldA_fieldC_idx", background: true }
)

// to remove indexes (review required)
// db.<collection>.dropIndex("old_index_name")

// Redundant index (review before delete)
// db.<collection>.dropIndex("redundant_index_name")

--------------------------------------------------

FINAL NOTE

- Script should be directly runnable in Mongo shell
- All destructive operations must be commented
- Clearly separate collections
- Add human-readable comments explaining each change

